    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="2" relname="condition">Intuitiveness is a concept, and if a design goal,</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="21" relname="span">needs to be tested in the early phases of design.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="19" relname="span">The UI part of development needs to be begin early in the lifecycle,</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="3" relname="antithesis">not saved for later (or never).</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="20" relname="span">Early testing is highly desirable over later testing.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="5" relname="nonvolitional-cause">Later testing in many cases, is just too late.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="18" relname="nonvolitional-cause">What developers may think is intuitive, is not at all to common users.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="22" relname="span">Most of the time, "intuitiveness" is used to market a product.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="23" relname="span">We see things like "This product is intuitive." or "On a scale of 1 -10, this product rates an 8 on intuitivness."</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="24" relname="span">These statements mean very little</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="10" relname="volitional-cause">because intuitiveness is not tested well or often enough.</segment>
        <segment id="12" parent="25" relname="span">The buzz word "intuitiveness" is most often used to sell, not to design.</segment>
        <segment id="13" parent="12" relname="evaluation">Big difference.</segment>
        <group id="14" type="span"/>
        <group id="15" type="multinuc" parent="14" relname="span"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="15" relname="contrast"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="16" relname="span"/>
        <group id="18" type="span" parent="17" relname="span"/>
        <group id="19" type="span" parent="18" relname="span"/>
        <group id="20" type="span" parent="19" relname="restatement"/>
        <group id="21" type="span" parent="17" relname="background"/>
        <group id="22" type="span" parent="15" relname="contrast"/>
        <group id="23" type="span" parent="8" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="24" type="span" parent="9" relname="evaluation"/>
        <group id="25" type="span" parent="15" relname="summary"/>
    </body>
